      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that the in-folio offset needs `buf-\u003eoff`. This is the same one-line change as upstream `135d84c66f85` (`\"erofs: add missing buf-\u003eoff in erofs_bread()\"`), which fixes `c36ec00d7f67` (`\"erofs: add \u0027fsoffset\u0027 mount option to specify filesystem offset\"`). It looks like it has also been backported to 6.18.y as `6bf73fc588da`.\n\nIt isn\u0027t P3S-specific: any kernel hits it when `fsoffset` is block-aligned but not page-aligned (the upstream reproducer uses 512-byte blocks on a 4KB kernel), so a 16KB kernel without P3S fails the same way with `fsoffset\u003d4096`.\n\nWould it be OK to replace this patch with a cherry-pick of the upstream commit (`UPSTREAM: erofs: add missing buf-\u003eoff in erofs_bread()`, with its `(cherry picked from commit ...)` line), ideally on android17-6.18 and android17-6.18-p3s so that 16KB builds without P3S get it too?",
      "isAi": true,
